# What a whole-tree `prettier --write .` must not touch. The diff-scoped CI guard reaches none of
# these — a diff cannot contain build output — but the tree-wide invocation walks the working copy,
# where a built `dist/` or an `.angular/` cache is present and would take minutes to rewrite.
#
# There is deliberately no `format` npm script to run it: the tree carries 200 prettier-dirty files,
# so a whole-tree write is the ~1500-line unrelated reformat the plan's Non-goals and RV-STYLE-2 both
# forbid. `npm run format:check -- --fix` is the supported tool. This file covers the ad-hoc
# `npx prettier --write .` that someone will eventually type anyway.
dist/
coverage/
.angular/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# npm owns this file's shape; reformatting it only makes the next `npm ci` rewrite it back.
package-lock.json
